Midday sweep October 31 2026, fired six hours after the early morning pass in a window where the two directory surfaces split cleanly: the mcpservers.org newest page came back through the r.jina.ai reader proxy with twelve unique slugs and every one of them sat inside the morning dispositions, so that page carried no delta, while the mcp.so recentServers block carried 30 parsed cards with the newest at 2026-10-31T14:37:33Z against 2026-10-31T03:22:19Z at the previous read, leaving exactly two cards above the morning stamp and both were read to detail level. The issue window moved more than either, twelve submissions landing on chatmcp/mcpso between #6499 at 11:19Z and #6510 at 16:42Z, and the whole window was read with bodies in one authenticated call rather than sampled from titles. One arrival was catalogued. MonitorBankRates MCP - https://mcp.monitorbankrates.com/mcp is remote Streamable HTTP and keyless, initialize answering HTTP 200 with serverInfo MonitorBankRates at 1.2.0 and tools/list returning all eight tools with full input schemas, so the surface was measured rather than quoted. Two calls measured the day: the national 12-month CD average at 3.0101 percent APY as of 2026-10-31 across 4,107 institutions and 9,115 quotes with change_1w of +0.019, and the high-yield savings average at 2.0501 percent APY across 271 institutions and 709 quotes. The dataset is every published rate at more than 8,000 US banks and credit unions recomputed daily, and the tools read it as best rates by product and geography, national and state averages with week, month and quarter change plus daily history, an institution directory carrying health grade, star rating and Texas ratio, mortgage lenders ranked by federal HMDA closings, loan and refinance calculators that return a breakeven in months, and three proprietary affordability and insurance burden indexes. It earns a guide because the treasury entries here read markets and none reads the deposit side of the balance sheet at institution level, which is where an operating balance actually sits. Held on class: numradar (a WhatsApp registration check, 401 behind a bearer key, four tools unpublished, paid-only from 9 dollars a month, the verification commodity already answered by the phone intelligence entry and the email verification trio, with an explicit promotion test recorded), mkts Market Data (15 read-only tools with provenance, in a stock and market data slice already carried by Altair, ValuEdge, fAlpha and BDE plus nine EDGAR surfaces), Signbee (second e-signature surface beside zsign #6415), doc2json (document extraction class), Avo Cado Read (reader class), GotSOL.app, Shellway Relay and web2mcp (agent payments and developer infrastructure), DiscoverLaunches, GitHubCard, The Charter Desk, Pokerai API, SlotVFX and AwesomeVideo. TradingCalc #6502 was an update request, not an arrival, and it reports that the mcp.so submission edit form does not save, the same fault as #5788, recorded as a platform defect. The five tracked listing surfaces were re-probed in the same pass: CorpusIQ is live on mcpservers.org at /servers/corpusiq-io, on Smithery as Cprusiq with unlisted false, and on Glama both as CorpusIQ/corpusiq-docs and as the connector io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp on the newer /mcp/connectors/ route, the official registry carries io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp as active with the mcp2.corpusiq.io remote, and mcp.so remains not listed with all four direct slugs at 404, the free route sign-in gated and the paid route declined. A fresh two-pass GitHub directory search ran 20 queries and returned 282 directory-style candidates with issues enabled, none of them a business-operations MCP directory that accepts an external submission. Counts: mcpservers.org /all proxy read 12 unique slugs, mcp.so recentServers 30 parsed cards, issue window #6499 to #6510, guide tree 1,069 server entries before this pass and 1,070 after, across 1,454 files. Supplement pass an hour later on the 11:00 MST tick,